:{{Диалог|undefined}} I heard you are looking for me?
::'''Asta:''' Yeah. I want you to investigate the source of the memetic virus that infected the Crackup Conch.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Crackup Conch?
:::'''Asta:''' It's one of our Curios. It looks like an ordinary conch, but when you get close, you can hear the dirty jokes coming from the inside.
:::'''Asta:''' As long as you hold your laughter, you can slowly obtain the secret power it contains. Of course, no one has succeeded so far, so we only use it on people in interrogations.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} "Memetic virus?"
:::'''Asta:''' It is a kind of information particle that spreads around exponentially like a virus, which will bring changes and contamination to the host's nature of thinking.
:::'''Asta:''' Unfortunately, it can infect inanimate objects, and thus it changed the Crackup Conch's external expression &mdash; it no longer tells jokes, but instead, it keeps talking weird nonsense.
:::'''Asta:''' Like "Get out of your comfort zone, or you'll be wasted," or "The pain you suffer will light up your way"... cliché quotes that just make people cringe.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Thank you for the explanation. I got the gist.
:::'''Asta:''' I had someone examine it and found that it was caused by the memetic virus. But the Crackup Conch has been properly stored all this time, which means it's impossible for it to get infected on its own.
:::'''Asta:''' The only possibility is that workers who were already infected passed on the virus when they came into contact with the item. After I looked into the list of people who had recent contact with it, I identified three suspects.
:::'''Asta:''' Well, I'm sure you already know what I'm about to say next. I want you to investigate these three suspects for me.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why me...
::::'''Asta:''' Hehe, with great power comes great responsibility. Besides, I'm not just trying to take advantage of you. I sent people from the Security Department earlier, but they all failed.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Is the Security Department here just for show?
::::'''Asta:''' I arranged for them to investigate as soon as I identified the list of suspects. But they all found nothing unusual.
::::'''Asta:''' Since these suspects have spent a fair bit of time in the space station, they are pretty familiar with the Security Department. They might have gotten away with their possible misconduct.
:::'''Asta:''' I, therefore, could not get any useful investigation results. That's why I need to ask you for a favor &mdash; you don't know them very well. It may be easier for you to spot their flaws from a stranger's perspective.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} What if they find out?
::::'''Asta:''' Don't worry, you are a hero who has saved the space station. No one will suspect you.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Sounds reasonable...
::::'''Asta:''' It is!
::::'''Asta:''' And it is not rocket science. You just need to walk up to them and listen, then see if there are any unusual behaviors.
:::'''Asta:''' If you find anything weird, just write it down and report it to me. So, what do you think?
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} No problem. I'll take care of it.
::::'''Asta:''' That's great. I'm so relieved that you're willing to help. I will reward you fairly. Let me think...
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I can help, but are there any rewards...
::::'''Asta:''' Don't worry. Do you have anything in mind already? I heard the starnought fleet has been very popular recently. But that thing is huge. I don't think you'll like it...
:::'''Asta:''' Well... I don't know your taste. Why don't I pay for everything in your shopping cart out of my own pocket? You are free to choose whatever you like.
:::'''Asta:''' Well, let me tell you about the three suspects &mdash; Mare from the Department of Insight, Chris from the Department of Galactic Geopolitics, and Joanne from the Medical Department.
:::'''Asta:''' They usually stay in their own cabins. Given the station's current situation, I don't think they'll be anywhere else... So, please help me take care of this.
:::----
:::----
;(If )
:{{Диалог|undefined}} (Tell her your observation and your thoughts.)
::'''Asta:''' So, all three of them sound unusual. But in theory, there should only be one person who is infected.
::'''Asta:''' The principle behind it is actually quite simple. The viral load of informational particles left behind by the memetic virus in the Crackup Conch is simply not high enough.
::'''Asta:''' The viral load detected barely reaches the amount that can be carried by an infected adult. So it's absolutely impossible for the Crackup Conch to have contracted the virus from multiple individuals.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} But my investigation couldn't corroborate this...
:::'''Asta:''' It's okay. I've got a backup plan.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So, what next?
:::'''Asta:''' Hehe, I've got a backup plan.
::'''Asta:''' The memetic virus is transmitted through virtual data. And all the virtual data in the space station leave traces in the terminal.
::'''Asta:''' Since we couldn't get much from our previous investigation, let's check the browsing records of the three suspects. Then we should be able to identify the source of the infection.
::'''Asta:''' Hehe, I've got an emergency plan for situations like this. Please visit the Data Exchange Center &mdash; where the terminal is located.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} But I've never used a terminal...
:::'''Asta:''' Don't worry. It's simple. Enter the terminal room, verify your identity, and you can start your query.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why don't you go yourself?
:::'''Asta:''' *sigh* I have my own reasons. It's a long story.
::'''Asta:''' Simply put, anyone using any data gadget, which basically includes everyone on the space station, would have their user behaviors recorded by the terminal. It is thus inappropriate for me or any other staff member to check such information.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Um, I still don't get it.
:::'''Asta:''' Don't worry. I'll explain to you when I have time.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I know. You are just looking for excuses to slack off.
:::'''Asta:''' It's not like that. I would have gone if I could.
::'''Asta:''' Think about it. Despite different backgrounds and identities, people on the space station have reached an agreement on personal privacy.
::'''Asta:''' The traces left from using virtual data can be found on the terminal. For example, from here people can see all the unusual virtual platforms you visited during your working hours.
::'''Asta:''' Therefore, to respect everyone's privacy, no one, including myself and the other staff, should access the terminal.
::'''Asta:''' Think about it in their shoes, if you are space station staff, would you be happy with me going through your browsing records on the virtual network?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'd rather die...
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It's unacceptable.
::'''Asta:''' Now you understand, right? That's why your special identity makes you the perfect candidate for this!
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why? I don't understand.
:::'''Asta:''' Let me start with your heroic deeds and your special identity.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} So, you just want me to get beaten up?
:::'''Asta:''' Jeez, is this the kind of nonsense you think about all day? I have nothing against you. Why would I set you up?
::'''Asta:''' From an objective point of view, you are an outsider on the space station. You are not familiar with most people here, so it's unlikely that you hold any personal grudge against anyone.
::'''Asta:''' Not every outsider has the right to access the data records. But you are different. You are the hero who saved the space station. People trust your moral character.
::'''Asta:''' But of course, if you do decide to help, I hope you will keep everything you see strictly confidential.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} No problem. My lips are sealed.
:::'''Asta:''' Anyway, keep it all a secret while you're still in the space station. As for where you go or what you do in the future, it's none of my business.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Piece of cake. Just leave it to me.
:::'''Asta:''' Thank you so much!
::'''Asta:''' Before you leave, let me tell you how to use the terminal.
::'''Asta:''' As you know, the invasion of the station severely damaged the whole data center. And the server room where the terminal is housed is no exception.
::'''Asta:''' Despite our best efforts, the damage is yet to be fully remediated. And reported cases of memetic virus infection only made things worse. I had to send a maintenance engineer to monitor the situation on a daily basis.
::'''Asta:''' {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|The engineer would turn on the optical identity verification program manually every day}} to check whether the bioelectricity of each visitor entering the room is normal, thus ensuring that the terminal room is not invaded.
::'''Asta:''' Since the optical identity verification program is {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|refreshed dynamically after it is turned on every day, you need to re-verify your identity every time you enter.}}
::'''Asta:''' For more details, please {{Цвет|Ключевой|nobold=1|consult the maintenance engineer}}. I've told the engineer that you have permission to enter the room.
::'''Asta:''' So... I will leave the rest to you!
::----
::----
;(If )
:{{Диалог|undefined}} I've gone through all the data records.
::'''Asta:''' Great. I heard from the maintenance engineer that, due to incomplete recovery from the previous invasion, the terminal's computing power had been hindering your progress.
::'''Asta:''' So I didn't expect you to finish the investigation so soon. Thank you for your hard work. So what's the conclusion?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} (Tell her your observation and your analysis.)
::'''Asta:''' Haha, I see. I did have a suspicion that Joanne was the one who got infected. But I didn't have any substantial evidence.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} How did you know it was her?
:::'''Asta:''' Simple. Out of the three of them, she is the only one who exhibited speech patterns similar to those of the Crackup Conch after its infection.
:::'''Asta:''' I've always found it rather suspicious that she, a person who dozes off all the time, would have such a drastic change of personality and would quit all her habits and hobbies out of nowhere.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Have you ever suspected the other two?
:::'''Asta:''' Their behaviors may seem strange to you, but to me, they are extremely normal.
:::'''Asta:''' Let's start with Mare. Getting distracted at work is such a common occurrence for all humans. It sometimes happens to me, even when I'm working in my favorite field of research.
:::'''Asta:''' Then there's Chris. He is said to be a good student from a poor family. And compared with the other researchers, he's still fairly new here on the space station. So it's normal that he would experience discomfort after a lengthy space flight.
:::'''Asta:''' What surprised me was the severity of his discomfort. So I've already sent for a doctor to check on him.
::'''Asta:''' Anyway, the overall result is as expected. Next, we should weed out Joanne's virus and get her "back on track" to her old self.
::'''Asta:''' Thank you for your hard work on finding such substantial evidence, so&mdash;
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Hold on, I have a few questions.
:::'''Asta:''' Oh? Go ahead. I'll answer all your questions if I know the answers.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I still don't get it...
:::'''Asta:''' Huh?
::'''Asta:''' Is there anything else I need to clarify?
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Isn't it a good thing to keep Joanne this way?
:::'''Asta:''' ...That was a dangerous thought. Of course not. Joanne is a living human being. You shouldn't think like that.
:::'''Asta:''' Although we come from different cultural backgrounds, some of the most basic rights and interests are recognized by all of us as the common bottom line and must not be deprived.
:::'''Asta:''' Besides, based on my personal experience, you'll never get great results in any field of research unless you are passionate about it.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} How did you guess correctly that Joanne was the one?
:::'''Asta:''' Guess? I didn't "guess." To some extent, it was just simple psychology.
:::'''Asta:''' Joanne completely wiped out her personal life, which is very unusual. Think about this simple analogy. People's capacity for work is limited, just like how a balloon can only hold a finite amount of air...
:::'''Asta:''' When they don't get enough rest or fulfillment, people will just be like a balloon being unceasingly inflated, which will inevitably blow up if there's no chance for an air release.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Aren't you worried about the other two?
:::'''Asta:''' Worried about what? Do you mean how their research at the space station will be affected? I don't think there's any problem except that Chris might need some psychological counseling from a doctor.
:::'''Asta:''' People have the freedom to do whatever they want in their own lives, as long as they don't undermine the security of the space station or violate the regulations.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I don't have any more questions.
:::'''Asta:''' Well, I do get your point to some extent. It might seem productive, at least in the short term, to just disregard people's safety concerns and force them into nonstop work. But in the real world, such practices will only spell disaster.
:::'''Asta:''' The station is built in space, far away from any land surface. Not everyone can adapt to life here. This will become clear after a while.
:::'''Asta:''' Despite our top-notch equipment and resources, some people still find it unbearable to live on the station after staying here for a long time.
:::'''Asta:''' In that case, letting people develop their own hobbies improves everyone's mental health, especially when they have been away from land for an extended period of time. This is the best way to improve overall productivity.
:::'''Asta:''' After all, we are born to be humans, not plants or rocks that do not have emotions. How could we still call ourselves humans if we were to throw away our hobbies and emotions?
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} But I don't seem to have any hobbies...
::::'''Asta:''' Well, I do know a little about your situation. It's alright. You still have a long way to go. You'll eventually find your hobbies and your own way of life.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} That makes sense.
::::'''Asta:''' Of course it does. This is also my life experience. Having fun in life is all about investing in things that you find interesting.
:::'''Asta:''' Well, you still have a long way ahead of you. When you are out there exploring, remember &mdash; no matter what, don't just throw away your hobbies and your emotions.
:::'''Asta:''' Oh right, by the way, I almost forgot one thing.
:::'''Asta:''' I know paper records will be printed out at the terminal. Keep those records to yourself. Don't let the information leak out in the space station. Promise me, or I'll take back the reward.
:::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Don't worry, they will never leak out.
:::'''Asta:''' Well, anyway, thank you so much. This is the reward for you. I made this myself.
